.TH FORTIGATE-AI-AGENT 1 "JULY 2026" "v1.0.0" "FortiGate AI Agent Manual"
.SH NAME
fortigate-ai-agent \- AI-powered diagnostics and operations CLI for FortiGate firewalls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 main.py
[\fIcommand\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fortigate-ai-agent
is an agentic CLI utility powered by Gemini. It connects to the FortiOS REST API to perform automatic system health diagnostics, interface reviews, VPN audits, and routing lookups. 
The tool supports an interactive chat console, a structured silent JSON diagnostics reporter, and a high-fidelity offline simulation (Mock Mode).

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B diagnose
Run a comprehensive, real-time diagnostic suite. Fetches system status, resource usage, interfaces status, VPN connections, routing table, ARP mappings, DHCP leases, and event logs. Feeds all data to the Gemini agent to compile a security and health report. This is the default command if none is specified.
.TP
.B interactive
Enter an interactive console chat. Launches a stateful session where you can query the AI agent in real-time. The agent dynamically decides which REST API tools to execute to answer your queries.
.TP
.B agentic
Run an autonomous multi-step investigation loop with live tool execution tracing.
.TP
.B backup
Take a full configuration backup snapshot of the FortiGate firewall and save it locally in the .backups directory.
.TP
.B config
Inspect the current connection details, target VDOM, SSL settings, execution mode (Mock or Live), and Gemini model selection.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-json
Run diagnostics silently, bypassing ASCII headers and progress indicators. Enforces the AI agent to output the health analysis as a structured JSON object matching a strict Pydantic schema (ideal for pipelines and scripting).
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-mock
Force offline Mock Mode. Simulates high-fidelity FortiGate telemetry (e.g. CPU spikes, down interfaces, VPN pre-shared key negotiation failures) without making network requests.
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-enable\-write
Enable active write/mitigation actions (disabled by default for safety). Requires a REST API Admin key with write capabilities.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-dry\-run
Simulate write actions safely without modifying firewall configuration. Displays proposed parameters in a warning panel.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
Export diagnostic report to a standalone HTML (.html), Markdown (.md), or JSON (.json) file.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-ip \fIADDRESS\fR
Override target FortiGate IP address or hostname.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-token \fITOKEN\fR
Override FortiGate REST API Access Token.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-port \fIPORT\fR
Override API connection port (defaults to 443).
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-vdom \fIVDOM\fR
Override target Virtual Domain (defaults to "root").
.TP
.B \-k, \-\-verify\-ssl
Enable HTTPS SSL certificate verification.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-ca\-bundle \fIFILE\fR
Path to custom CA certificate bundle file (implicitly enables SSL verification).
.TP
.B \-\-model \fIMODEL\fR
Override target Gemini model (e.g. gemini-2.5-flash, gemini-2.5-pro, gemini-3.5-flash, gemini-pro-latest).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
The agent loads default settings from a local \fB.env\fR file or the system environment:
.TP
.B GEMINI_API_KEY
Required. Google Gemini Developer API key.
.TP
.B GEMINI_MODEL
Target Gemini model name (default is "gemini-2.5-flash").
.TP
.B FORTIGATE_IP
IP address or hostname of the FortiGate firewall.
.TP
.B FORTIGATE_TOKEN
REST API Admin key generated on the FortiGate GUI.
.TP
.B FORTIGATE_PORT
Target HTTPS/HTTP port (default is 443).
.TP
.B FORTIGATE_VDOM
Target Virtual Domain name (default is "root").
.TP
.B USE_SSL
Boolean (True/False) to enable HTTPS protocol (default is True).
.TP
.B VERIFY_SSL
Boolean (True/False) to verify SSL certificates (default is False).
.TP
.B CA_BUNDLE
Path to CA certificate bundle (.pem) file.
.TP
.B MOCK_MODE
Boolean (True/False) to force offline mock simulation.
.TP
.B ENABLE_WRITE_ACTIONS
Boolean (True/False) to enable active configuration write/mitigation actions (default is False).
.TP
.B DRY_RUN
Boolean (True/False) to simulate configuration write actions safely without sending REST requests to the firewall (default is False).
.TP
.B BACKUP_BEFORE_WRITE
Boolean (True/False) to automatically create a configuration snapshot backup before applying write operations (default is True).
.TP
.B OUTPUT_FILE
Path to export report output file (.html, .md, or .json).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I .env
Local environment configuration file.
.TP
.I fortigate_agent.log
Execution trace log documenting all HTTP requests, parameters, retry attempts, and AI tool invocations.
.TP
.I fortigate-ai-agent.1
Nroff/troff source file for this manual page.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run automated diagnostics in Mock Mode:
.B python3 main.py diagnose --mock
.TP
Interrogate your firewall interactively about active VPN users:
.B python3 main.py interactive --ip 192.168.1.99 --token my_token
.TP
Silent diagnostics piping JSON report into jq parser:
.B python3 main.py --json --mock | jq .
.TP
View configuration status:
.B python3 main.py config
.TP
Run interactive agent allowing mitigation write actions:
.B python3 main.py interactive --enable-write

.SH BUGS
Log issues or review code execution tracks inside the local \fBfortigate_agent.log\fR file.

